WHO   — TARDIGRADES — a life-science sphere — the brainless mind
WHAT  — Dry one out and it shrivels to a lifeless grain — metabolism falling to nothing, the line between living and dead simply gone. Years later, add water, and it walks away. The tardigrade can switch itself off and survive boiling, freezing, crushing pressure, and the open vacuum of space, then switch back on. Not life ending and beginning, but life paused.
WHERE — intelligence without a brain  Framework inputs: the living; the rule; the signal; the open question  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Dry one out and it shrivels to a lifeless grain — metabolism falling to nothing, the line between living and dead simply gone. Years later, add water, and it walks away. The tardigrade can switch itself off and survive boiling, freezing, crushing pressure, and the open vacuum of space, then switch back on. Not life ending and beginning, but life paused.
HOW   — Crystallized from the public record of the science.

